Q: INSERT a new row for each word in a submitted comma-separated string using CodeIgniter A: <p>Chances are that there is no benefit to storing duplicate keywords, so I'll recommend a schema which will makes a single trip to the database, rejects duplicates, contains primary keys, and auto-populates the create datetime stamps.</p>
<p>I don't know if your script is in the controller or model layer, but controller methods should interact with the database and models shouldn't directly access submission payloads.</p>
<p>If you actually want to record the popularity of keywords, then you could define a tallying column (<code>kp_count INT UNSIGNED NOT NULL DEFAULT 1</code>) and append <code>ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE kp_count = kp_count + 1</code> to the INSERT query, but I don't know if this is your intention.</p>
<p>The recommended table schema: <a href="https://sqlize.online/sql/mysql80/2e3ab507b3c6f78f686b5ccccdcc43a7/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">SQLize Demo</a></p>
<pre class="lang-sql prettyprint-override"><code>CREATE TABLE keyword_popular (
    kp_id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,
    kp_keyword VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    kp_created_on DATETIME NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
) ENGINE=InnoDB;
</code></pre>
<p>Your controller:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>public function saveKeywords()
{
    $keywords = array_filter(
        array_unique(
            array_map(
                'trim',
                explode(',', mb_strtolower($this-&gt;input-&gt;post('keyword') ?? ''))
            )
        )
    );

    $this-&gt;load-&gt;model('Keyword_model');
    $this-&gt;Keyword_model-&gt;save($keywords);
}
</code></pre>
<p>The model:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>class Keyword_model extends CI_Model
{
    protected string $table = 'keyword_popular';

    public function __construct()
    {
        parent::__construct();
    }

    public function save(array $keywords): void
    {
        if (!$keywords) {
            return;
        }

        $this-&gt;db-&gt;query(
            &quot;INSERT IGNORE INTO {$this-&gt;table} (kp_keyword) VALUES &quot;
                . implode(',', array_fill(0, count($keywords), '(?)')),
            $keywords
        );
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Topically relevant reading: <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/79806918/2943403">How to INSERT or UPDATE a record in CodeIgniter depending on if the record already exists</a></p>
